. LESSON 10 SWAP MODULES
. In these examples color 1 is teal, not red. $L1 says which of the
. palette's 256 colors color 1 shows (lesson 7); 29 is teal, and
. $L1=1 makes it red again.
$L1=29
. A swap module is a program loaded from tape. The lesson's is TXT,
. which writes numbers and letters on the TV, and GETTAPE TXT loads it.
. There is no tape and no TXT here, so XYAXES puts tick marks where TXT
. wrote the numbers.
XYAXES=[LINE 160,-80,4
LINE -140,-80,1
LINE -140,100,1
X=-140;N=0
LINE X,-80,4;LINE X,-85,1;X=X+20
IF (N=N+1)<15,SKIP -1
Y=-80;N=0
LINE -140,Y,4;LINE -145,Y,1;Y=Y+20
IF (N=N+1)<10,SKIP -1]

. THE ANIMATION. SCOPE draws XYAXES and then a wave over and over, left
. to right, like an oscilloscope. Just ahead of the pen a narrow box
. blacks out the last pass, so the old wave is replaced as the new one
. is drawn. The wave is two sines, and as it starts each pass where the
. last left off, it seems to move. The node's Stop button stops it, and Play carries on.
SCOPE=[CLEAR;XYAXES;A=0
1PASS X=-138;LINE X,10+SIN(A)*40+SIN(A*3)*20,4
BOX X+4,11,6,180,0;LINE X,10+SIN(A)*40+SIN(A*3)*20,3;A=A+3
IF (X=X+1)<159,SKIP -1
GOTO 1PASS]
SCOPE
